this ascension is dedicated to the lady robin,
without whose conscientious (and repeated) efforts
i would have fallen to the dark Trickery.

this is my first ever chaotic ascension, and i've
now got a "lifetime double top". i spent many
weeks over the course of previous tournaments
slinging daggers because i've always wanted to
ascend a rogue, but usually fall back to my old
archaeologist before the end.

I started this game three weeks ago, of course,
(dear lord, and almost five days of realtime
gaming? that must be fore the times i dozed off
at the keyboard...) and didn't keep notes, so the
early details are foggy. I think I hit a total of
three bones files, however. I found a very early
magic lamp, but kept it for the light all the way
to the astral plain before spending it on my
initial boulder.

i remember many early altars, which i usually
don't get. and my second puppy rambled into a
polymorph trap and became a trusted balrog
companion who got me through many tough spots
in the lower levels before succumbing to a purple
worm in hell. i had intended on going poly-less
as well as the polypile-less that i did
achieve, but that same trap got me before i saw
my new balrog. <snif> poor lil' guy. i miss him.

i really wanted grayswandir or frostbrand or
magicbane, but then level twenty held three
artifacts, so wishing for those wasn't happening,
and i stuck with firebrand. (ironically, the
first player monster on the astral plain held
frosty)

The turning point, of course, was running into
nailbunny's black pudding farm on level 20. he
died in a doorway, so it wasn't readily apparent
how he died, and i haven't scoured the score files
yet to find out. not having ever seen an actual
functioning farm before, it was scary, the whole
level completely cleared of walls, lit up, and
maybe 60% full of black goo. but there were close
to ten magic markers on the altar, and nothing was
too terribly challenging with that boost.

so, i dove down, lured most of the baddies down the
holes in the castle to deal with later in the valley
so that i could get the wand and round out my kit.
i must say, silver daggers are things of beauty. I
had 18 of them at +6 by the end. who needs
grayswandir when you manage to start all the big
demon fights with four silver spikes sizzling in
demonic flesh?

blah blah blah - many magic mappings later, i made
the run without anything notable. only got yanked
backwards once on the way out of hell. stopped at
my cache and kept going. got an iron golem pet on
level five, somehow, i think, and he my be floating
somewhere on the water plane still for all i know.

the astral plane, of course, is where the game
really started. my intent this time was to kill
death many times, but i didn't bother to check
which was which, and by the time i'd made it to the
second alter and Kos, there were at least four
archons and a titan between him and me, so i decided
not to press my luck.

but i'd never really had my contact with Famine, so
i was tentative, as i set up my machine. i needn't have
worried. I don't know what people worry about--even
when my AC dropped to -20, he never got me even down
to Hungry or below 90% of MaxHP. Pestilence got me
much closer to doom last year and the year before.

The worst moment ingame was after Famine woke up at
the same time an archon appeared, with me in Xorn
form on a boulder between the two of them. I popped
back into half-naked human form, but due to the xorn
'bug' that gets you stuck in a nonexistent pit, i
couldn't get off the square for something like three
resurrections. the first time it said "Your leg gets
stuck in a crevice," my heart fluttered, though.

Worse than that, though, was the strange game
corruption stuff last weekend. my ssh client crashed,
and when i tried to come back, my save wouldn't load.
eventually robin, blessings upon her, got it working,
but the file wouldn't save, so i had to finish in one
session. it's odd to say a gametime of 5 days was
"cut short", but so it goes.

i do carry on, given the chance. i'll refrain from
screendumps here, as it's nothing special.

cheers to all, and many thanks to Robin and the other
admins for their dedication. oh, and to nailbunny.   :)



